<title>CHINA: China short up to 250,000T zinc on LME - CNNC.</title>
<headline>China short up to 250,000T zinc on LME - CNNC.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>China is short up to 250,000 tonnes of zinc on the London Metal Exchange (LME), an official of the government's metals production arm China National Nonferrous Metals Corp (CNNC) said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not made detailed calculations, but the position ... is about 200,000 to 250,000 tonnes,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We will consider helping the zinc smelters to extricate themselves from the trouble, such as reaching a balance among different smelters,&quot; the official said.</p>
</text>
